# meet of semipredicates, defined by the truth table:
#       | TOP  I  BOT
#   ----+------------
#   TOP | TOP TOP TOP
#    I  | TOP  I  BOT
#   BOT | TOP BOT BOT
# Note unlike JOIN which is a join on the whole space, MEET is a meet operation
# only on the space any -> [BOT, I], hence the rules below are weaker than the
# JOIN rules.

# definition: meet = (\x:any->semi,y:any->semi. S x y | S y x).
EQUAL MEET x y JS COMP SEMI x COMP SEMI y
EQUAL JS JOIN S APP C S

CLOSED x   CLOSED y
-------------------
  CLOSED MEET x y

OPTIONALLY EQUAL MEET x y MEET y x
EQUAL MEET x MEET y z MEET MEET x y z

       LESS y z          LESS x y         LESS x z
----------------------   -------------------------
LESS MEET x y MEET x z   LESS MEET y z COMP SEMI x

EQUAL MEET KI x COMP SEMI x
EQUAL MEET TOP x TOP
EQUAL MEET x x COMP SEMI x

# FIXME these rules fail for y = TOP.
# We need to somehow include COMP APP CB BOT COMP SEMI y
# LESS MEET x y COMP SEMI x 
# EQUAL MEET BOT y BOT
# 
#          LESS x y
# --------------------------
# EQUAL MEET x y COMP SEMI x
